## 6. States and Interactions

### 6.1 Element States

| State    | Visual Change                     |
| -------- | --------------------------------- |
| Hover    | Background color change, shadow emphasis |
| Focus    | Blue outline (#4B73FF)            |
| Active   | Color change, visual marker (e.g., left line) |
| Disabled | Opacity reduction (0.5)           |

### 6.2 Animations

- **Transition Time**: 0.2s - 0.3s
- **Easing**: ease-in-out
- **Applicable Elements**: Hover states, expand/collapse, element show/hide

### 6.3 Feedback

- **Button Click**: Slight press effect (scale 0.98)
- **Save Complete**: Success message display (green)
- **Error**: Error message display (red)
- **Loading**: Progress indicator or spinner

## 7. Responsive Design

### 7.1 Breakpoints

- **Small**: Below 768px
- **Medium**: 768px - 1024px
- **Large**: Above 1024px

### 7.2 Responsive Behavior

- **Sidebar**: Overlay mode on small screens
- **Splitter**: Changes to vertical layout on small screens
- **Toolbar**: Wraps to multiple lines on small screens
- **Settings Panel**: Modal display on small screens

## 8. Accessibility

### 8.1 Color Contrast

- Text always maintains WCAG AA standard (4.5:1) contrast ratio or higher.
- Large text (18px and above) maintains a 3:1 contrast ratio or higher.

### 8.2 Keyboard Navigation

- All interactive elements are focusable via Tab key.
- Focus state is always visually clear (blue outline).
- Assign shortcut keys to important functions.

### 8.3 ARIA Support

- Use appropriate ARIA roles and attributes.
- Provide alternative text for screen reader compatibility.
- Appropriately notify changes in dynamic content.

